:- module(macro_decls_wildcard).

% A `_` passed to a declaration macro is one variable shared by every
% copy of that argument: the generated rule joins a and b.
:- chr_type answer ---> yes ; no.
:- chr_constraint a/1, b/1, hit/0, ask/1.
:- macro_decls mk(X) ---> [(a(X), b(X) ==> hit)].
:- mk(_).

hit \ ask(R) <=> R = yes.
ask(R) <=> R = no.

:- chr_constraint test/2.
test(X, R) <=> a(1), b(X), ask(R).
